Subject: [PATCH] e2fsck: preserve errors found before read-only passes

In e2fsprogs 1.47.3, check_super_block clears filesystem validity when a
group descriptor checksum is invalid. The second ext2fs_mark_valid call
discards that result before the main passes, so e2fsck -fn can report the
checksum error and still exit successfully.

Keep the initial validity state when -n disables repairs. The first
initialization before check_super_block remains unchanged. Repair modes
retain the second reset because their passes can repair the detected errors.

--- a/e2fsck/unix.c
+++ b/e2fsck/unix.c
@@ -1898 +1898 @@
-	 * Mark the system as valid, 'til proven otherwise
+	 * Preserve errors found before the main passes when fixes are disabled.
@@ -1900 +1900,2 @@
-	ext2fs_mark_valid(fs);
+	if (!(ctx->options & E2F_OPT_NO))
+		ext2fs_mark_valid(fs);
